### Git:
Git is a powerful tool that constantly keeps track of every changes you make to your files.
( What changed?, Where changed?, When changed?, Who changed? )
Git != GitHub (they are connected, but not same)

### Git versions:
Git lets you keep different versions of same file effortlessly.
You can rollback to any previous versions in a moment.

### Diff. b/w Git &GitHub:

Git is a tool that locally runs on your own computer.
GitHub is a cloud-based platform where you can host Git repositories, store your code remotely, and collaborate with other developers.

